WEBVTT

00:00.007 --> 00:01.174
THIS IS A WORK OF FICTION. UNDERAGE
DRINKING IS STRONGLY PROHIBITED.

00:01.175 --> 00:02.467
FORCEFUL ALCOHOL CONSUMPTION, BINGE
DRINKING, SHAMEFUL ACTS NOT ENCOURAGED.

00:02.468 --> 00:03.760
VIEW THIS AS A COMEDY. ALL CHARACTERS
APPEARING IN THIS WORK ARE OF LEGAL AGE.

00:03.761 --> 00:04.970
DUE TO RECENT COMPLIANCE ISSUES, THE
BLACK DOT SIZE HAS BEEN INCREASED BY 5%.

00:16.106 --> 00:18.566
Let's go take a trip
under the bright summer sun

00:18.567 --> 00:21.778
GRAND BLUE DREAMING SEASON 3To a city far away, what do you say?

00:21.779 --> 00:24.197
Let's go take a trip
under the bright summer sun

00:24.198 --> 00:27.743
To a city far away, what do you say?

00:31.830 --> 00:33.706
Wait a sec, another heatwave?

00:33.707 --> 00:35.416
Temperatures are rising... Huh?!

00:35.417 --> 00:38.628
Our original plans are
totally busted, what now?

00:38.629 --> 00:41.464
But honestly, I'm getting so hyped

00:41.465 --> 00:44.133
Alright, let's roll up
our sleeves and dive in

00:44.134 --> 00:45.885
Rub your sleepy eyes and jump up

00:45.886 --> 00:47.345
Grab the usual shades

00:47.346 --> 00:50.265
Check your gear: Iced coffee, thermos

00:50.266 --> 00:52.934
Clear blue skies, just a trick of summer

00:52.935 --> 00:56.063
The booming speakers
keep calling my name

00:56.397 --> 00:58.899
Even now, I still believe

01:01.819 --> 01:03.778
In unexpected encounters

01:03.779 --> 01:06.364
And the miracles of this season

01:06.365 --> 01:09.617
Summer brings
those swing swing emotions

01:09.618 --> 01:12.370
Ah, even if I get a little carried away

01:12.371 --> 01:17.584
On my mind,
I've only been searching for you

01:17.585 --> 01:23.506
Let the south wind blow you here,
just as you are

01:23.507 --> 01:28.220
Under the blue sky, hold me tight

01:29.054 --> 01:34.476
I want to dream
a summer dream with you

01:37.438 --> 01:40.524
In the summer
of my first year of high school...

01:40.983 --> 01:43.027
I lost my V-card.

01:43.277 --> 01:44.861
- Huh?
- Huh?

01:44.862 --> 01:46.614
Hey, what's with that attitude?

01:46.864 --> 01:48.741
Well, because...

01:49.199 --> 01:51.743
Listening to someone yap about
their dream last night

01:51.744 --> 01:53.203
is the most pointless thing.

01:53.537 --> 01:53.578
MECHANICAL ENGINEERING DEPARTMENT LABORATORY NO. 2

01:53.579 --> 01:55.872
MECHANICAL ENGINEERING DEPARTMENT LABORATORY NO. 2
REMEDIAL CLASS IN SESSION Who said it was a dream?

01:55.873 --> 01:56.248
MECHANICAL ENGINEERING DEPARTMENT LABORATORY NO. 2

01:56.624 --> 01:58.124
This is a true story

01:58.125 --> 02:01.169
about Elena-san, the college student
who came to tutor me.

02:01.170 --> 02:02.962
You think you're in an AV or something?

02:02.963 --> 02:04.547
Or a porn game?

02:04.548 --> 02:06.175
No, no, it's true.

02:06.592 --> 02:10.179
If Elena-san were here,
she could prove that it's true.

02:11.513 --> 02:13.097
Well, that's a shame.

02:13.098 --> 02:15.517
I have a story like that too.

02:16.060 --> 02:16.644
Huh?

02:16.810 --> 02:17.978
Let's hear it.

02:18.520 --> 02:22.315
In middle school, I was so popular
I even had my own fan club.

02:22.316 --> 02:26.152
Huh? Stop bluffing!

02:26.153 --> 02:27.779
Are you even able to say that?

02:27.780 --> 02:31.324
If my middle school mates were here,
then I could prove it.

02:31.325 --> 02:33.911
Talk is cheap.

02:34.244 --> 02:37.163
What? Don't you guys have
any glorious tales like that?

02:37.164 --> 02:39.332
Well well, what a sad life.

02:39.333 --> 02:40.583
Stop talking nonsense!

02:40.584 --> 02:42.294
Of course we do!

02:42.670 --> 02:46.172
In elementary school, I was so
outstanding I was called a prodigy.

02:46.173 --> 02:48.425
And I was famous in my hometown.

02:48.550 --> 02:50.176
Oh, is that so?

02:50.177 --> 02:51.845
Smells like bullshit.

02:52.012 --> 02:53.430
- What did you say!?
- What did you say!?

02:54.056 --> 02:57.267
You guys are being too loud!

02:58.519 --> 03:00.937
This is my sacred lecture.

03:00.938 --> 03:03.899
Use this preparation time seriously.

03:04.608 --> 03:07.444
- But Associate Professor...
- These two are bullshitting!

03:07.569 --> 03:08.986
I told you it's not a lie.

03:08.987 --> 03:10.280
Envy is an ugly thing.

03:10.781 --> 03:11.990
Lying?

03:13.492 --> 03:16.536
Can't you guys see through
things like that?

03:16.537 --> 03:18.664
No, we can see right through it.

03:18.789 --> 03:20.958
It's just that they refuse to admit it.

03:21.917 --> 03:23.001
If that's the case,

03:23.419 --> 03:26.254
prove it the way that's worthy
of science students.

03:26.255 --> 03:28.132
- Worthy of science students?
- What do you mean?

03:29.633 --> 03:31.635
LIE DETECTOR (1980 YEN)

03:31.760 --> 03:33.302
No way, Associate Professor.

03:33.303 --> 03:35.389
Isn't this just a toy?

03:35.597 --> 03:37.807
Using this can be considered proving?

03:37.808 --> 03:39.267
Such fools.

03:39.268 --> 03:40.227
Huh?

03:40.769 --> 03:43.312
Do you know
the mechanism of this thing?

03:43.313 --> 03:44.689
MECHANISM OF LIE DETECTOR (1980 YEN)
It measures the subject's

03:44.690 --> 03:46.482
MECHANISM OF LIE DETECTOR (1980 YEN)
blood pressure and heart rate.

03:46.483 --> 03:49.694
I HAVE NO INTEREST IN ANIME
And detects lies by reading those changes.

03:49.695 --> 03:50.154
BZZ!! LIE

03:50.404 --> 03:52.656
But it's useless against these guys.

03:52.781 --> 03:55.867
They lie more naturally than breathing.

03:55.868 --> 03:57.952
I know that.

03:57.953 --> 04:00.664
Here's the talent of the
Mechanical Engineering department.

04:00.914 --> 04:02.623
LIE DETECTOR
CHARPY IMPACT TEST TYPE

04:02.624 --> 04:07.254
This way, we will increase
the psychological pressure of deceit.

04:07.546 --> 04:09.714
As expected of our professor!

04:09.715 --> 04:12.676
With this, it won't be easy to lie.

04:13.218 --> 04:16.012
Let's test how it works just in case.

04:16.013 --> 04:17.388
Alright, Yamamoto.

04:17.389 --> 04:18.890
Try telling a random lie.

04:18.891 --> 04:19.766
Me?

04:19.767 --> 04:21.184
Anything is fine.

04:21.185 --> 04:23.103
Asking me out of nowhere,

04:24.480 --> 04:27.399
I've never lied before...

04:35.491 --> 04:37.742
Hmm, it works normally.

04:37.743 --> 04:40.286
Excellent experimental machine as always.

04:40.287 --> 04:42.456
The destructive power is flawless too.

04:42.664 --> 04:45.833
I have many good points,
one of them is honesty...

04:45.834 --> 04:47.084
You don't need to lie now.

04:47.085 --> 04:48.962
The machine is reacting continuously.

04:49.379 --> 04:51.756
Then let's start with
the obvious lie first.

04:51.757 --> 04:52.508
Right.

04:52.633 --> 04:54.258
Come on, step up, Nojima.

04:54.259 --> 04:56.010
Who are you calling an clear liar?

04:56.011 --> 04:58.805
All of you, you dare to call me a fibber?

04:58.806 --> 04:59.722
So annoying!

04:59.723 --> 05:00.808
I'm going home!

05:02.768 --> 05:06.103
- No, can't do.
- We have to clarify the truth.

05:06.104 --> 05:07.980
Tsk.

05:07.981 --> 05:10.525
I wasn't planning on running away!

05:10.526 --> 05:11.609
Then what was that?

05:11.610 --> 05:14.738
I was just annoyed because you guys
treated me like a cheat.

05:15.781 --> 05:17.115
I see.

05:17.825 --> 05:19.409
Then Kouhei, you try first.

05:20.160 --> 05:21.787
Whatever.

05:21.995 --> 05:23.121
You sure about this?

05:23.372 --> 05:24.413
Piece of cake.

05:24.414 --> 05:26.708
I just have to not lie, right?

05:26.875 --> 05:27.835
That's right.

05:28.335 --> 05:30.002
Then try saying something.

05:30.003 --> 05:30.587
Alright.

05:31.338 --> 05:33.799
Actually, until now
I've always kept quiet, but...

05:37.427 --> 05:38.386
Why...?

05:38.387 --> 05:40.304
Because you didn't keep quiet at all.

05:40.305 --> 05:41.597
You're just about to talk.

05:41.598 --> 05:43.766
Even that part is considered a lie?

05:43.767 --> 05:45.602
You have to skip the preamble!

05:46.687 --> 05:49.522
Then call me when you're done.

05:49.523 --> 05:50.898
Is this really okay?

05:50.899 --> 05:52.276
What about safety supervision?

05:52.442 --> 05:54.944
Damn you, Kitahara!
How dare you trick me...

05:54.945 --> 05:57.280
Don't take your anger out on others.

05:57.281 --> 05:59.073
Stop making excuses. It's unsightly.

05:59.074 --> 05:59.866
You guys,

05:59.867 --> 06:01.409
bring Kitahara in.

06:01.410 --> 06:02.743
Yes, sir!

06:02.744 --> 06:04.413
You bastards!

06:06.498 --> 06:07.623
Fine then.

06:07.624 --> 06:09.793
I just need to tell the truth, right?

06:09.960 --> 06:12.420
The truth is, in high school,

06:12.421 --> 06:13.714
regarding girlfri-

06:17.509 --> 06:18.843
Don't fall asleep!

06:18.844 --> 06:21.805
Did you have one or not?!
Spit it out before you die!

06:22.180 --> 06:24.599
Well, then it's Mitarai's turn next, right?

06:24.600 --> 06:25.391
Agreed.

06:25.392 --> 06:27.935
In middle school,
you supposedly had a fan club?

06:27.936 --> 06:29.270
Ah, yeah.

06:29.271 --> 06:32.106
Then could you prove that it's true?

06:32.107 --> 06:34.401
Literally betting your life on it.

06:35.652 --> 06:36.862
Alright.

06:37.613 --> 06:39.531
Then I'll start asking.

06:40.741 --> 06:43.993
In middle school,
were you really popular?

06:43.994 --> 06:45.329
Yes!

06:46.997 --> 06:48.873
Seems like it's true.

06:48.874 --> 06:50.125
- What!?
- What!?

06:50.250 --> 06:51.877
Ask in more detail.

06:52.252 --> 06:54.378
Did you get confessed to often?

06:54.379 --> 06:54.963
Yes.

06:55.631 --> 06:59.425
Next, did your fan club actually exist?

06:59.426 --> 07:00.093
Yes.

07:00.594 --> 07:01.427
Impossible!

07:01.428 --> 07:03.096
Is it the truth?

07:03.805 --> 07:06.224
Seriously, is that enough?

07:08.769 --> 07:11.479
Why would I lie
about something like that?

07:11.480 --> 07:12.731
Then who were those...

07:13.315 --> 07:14.399
Kitahara?

07:14.608 --> 07:17.401
Th... The fans were...

07:17.402 --> 07:20.030
The members of that fan club...

07:20.489 --> 07:22.950
were they women?

07:30.248 --> 07:31.666
Hey, Mitarai.

07:31.667 --> 07:33.251
Who exactly were your fans?

07:33.835 --> 07:34.753
Phew.

07:35.045 --> 07:35.837
All done.

07:36.046 --> 07:40.384
It's almost time for
the main character to appear, right?

07:47.265 --> 07:48.558
Let's summarize.

07:49.226 --> 07:52.312
This machine is not a lie detector.

07:52.562 --> 07:55.773
It merely measures
blood pressure and heart rate.

07:55.774 --> 07:58.527
It still reacts to pressure
other than lying.

07:59.236 --> 08:00.195
Which means...

08:01.113 --> 08:04.866
it's entirely possible to turn
the truth into a lie.

08:05.117 --> 08:08.452
Anyway, him losing his virginity
during summer is made up.

08:08.453 --> 08:10.454
Trying so hard to act tough
is a joke itself.

08:10.455 --> 08:13.458
In the end, Nojima is just
that kind of guy.

08:16.420 --> 08:17.379
And above all,

08:18.380 --> 08:21.425
you guys have smeared my pride!

08:22.050 --> 08:24.218
Hurry up, you braggart.

08:24.219 --> 08:26.679
Say "I lost my virginity."

08:26.680 --> 08:28.515
And then admit it's a lie.

08:28.807 --> 08:29.683
Alright.

08:31.018 --> 08:32.185
Actually...

08:32.602 --> 08:34.395
the story about losing my virginity in...

08:34.396 --> 08:36.523
the summer of my first year
of high school...

08:40.402 --> 08:42.529
is not true!

08:45.949 --> 08:48.325
Do you really want to deny
that you're a virgin that much?

08:48.326 --> 08:50.787
He clearly told the truth, but it still...

08:51.621 --> 08:53.956
Professor, this machine is flawed.

08:53.957 --> 08:56.625
It's going off from a pulse
even while holding my breath.

08:56.626 --> 08:59.170
Because of that,
the truth can be seen as a lie.

08:59.171 --> 09:00.005
Hmm.

09:00.464 --> 09:01.964
I'll keep that in mind.

09:01.965 --> 09:03.008
GRAND BLUE DREAMING SEASON 3

09:06.011 --> 09:07.511
Hello, Kitahara?

09:07.512 --> 09:09.096
Nojima, what's up?

09:09.097 --> 09:11.433
Let me copy the assignment
that's due tomorrow.

09:11.767 --> 09:14.018
You haven't done it yet?

09:14.019 --> 09:16.313
I thought it was due next week.

09:16.688 --> 09:19.815
Anyway, I'm heading over to your place.
Let me borrow your report.

09:19.816 --> 09:21.318
Huh? To my place?

09:21.443 --> 09:23.986
Ah, wait, Nojima. It's not
a good time for me right now...

09:23.987 --> 09:24.987
It's fine.

09:24.988 --> 09:27.657
I don't mind if your room is messy.

09:27.866 --> 09:28.617
Huh?

09:29.034 --> 09:29.910
Oh?

09:30.452 --> 09:32.412
Are you Iori-kun's friend?

09:33.246 --> 09:35.457
Kitahara-kun?

09:35.791 --> 09:38.459
I'll do whatever you want.
Just spare my life.

09:38.460 --> 09:40.504
MUMBO JUMBO IZAKAYA

09:40.670 --> 09:42.005
So that's what happened.

09:42.506 --> 09:45.133
Kitahara helped us organize this mixer.

09:45.509 --> 09:47.511
What an amazing friendship.

09:47.803 --> 09:48.970
Bravo.

09:49.763 --> 09:52.349
Although I was tortured
for five hours straight.

09:52.641 --> 09:54.184
And what about the women?

09:55.268 --> 09:57.312
Nanaka-san will help find them.

09:57.854 --> 10:00.272
I just had to invite
some close friends, right?

10:00.273 --> 10:01.817
I'm counting on you.

10:03.193 --> 10:04.277
Good evening.

10:06.696 --> 10:08.323
You guys are early.

10:10.784 --> 10:12.410
You picked so fast!

10:12.702 --> 10:15.329
Isn't she my angel?

10:15.330 --> 10:17.499
Whose angel are you calling her?

10:19.793 --> 10:22.921
I have found the angel of my life.

10:24.506 --> 10:28.093
I haven't even named our children yet.

10:28.343 --> 10:30.678
Stop having dirty fantasies
about my wife.

10:30.679 --> 10:32.013
She's mine!

10:32.222 --> 10:34.015
Listen to me carefully.

10:34.432 --> 10:38.186
If you dare try anything with Nanaka-san,
I'll seriously murder you.

10:41.898 --> 10:43.233
That's fine.

10:44.526 --> 10:48.363
If I can get close to such a beauty
in exchange for my life...

10:48.697 --> 10:49.865
I'd gladly give it!

10:51.700 --> 10:54.285
Don't worry. I'll bring her happiness!

10:54.286 --> 10:55.870
I'll never make her cry!

10:55.871 --> 10:58.206
I'll treasure her for the rest of my life!

10:59.291 --> 11:00.292
You guys...

11:00.792 --> 11:01.626
Oh my.

11:03.128 --> 11:04.212
Am I late?

11:06.840 --> 11:08.424
"For the rest of my life," huh!?

11:08.425 --> 11:10.385
Have you invited Azusa-san as well?

11:10.552 --> 11:12.303
Yeah, and also...

11:12.304 --> 11:12.887
JUNIOR

11:12.888 --> 11:13.805
Hello.

11:14.347 --> 11:16.307
LITTLE SISTER

11:16.308 --> 11:18.310
MITARAI'S GIRLFRIEND

11:20.478 --> 11:21.771
Huh? Why?

11:22.397 --> 11:24.149
She's a friend of Aina-chan.

11:24.316 --> 11:26.735
This is my new friend, Rie Oohashi.

11:27.110 --> 11:29.863
Hello, mind if I join for a bit?

11:30.572 --> 11:31.865
Just for a bit?

11:31.990 --> 11:32.657
That's right.

11:33.074 --> 11:35.619
Until the prey falls into the trap.

11:36.661 --> 11:37.454
Oh my.

11:37.746 --> 11:39.288
YU MITARAIIs there a mixer tonight?

11:39.289 --> 11:41.124
YU MITARAII'm almost there. Wait for me!

11:42.042 --> 11:44.627
No one invited you.
It's better if you don't come.

11:44.628 --> 11:46.213
Don't joke around.

11:46.379 --> 11:49.174
Tonight I will turn into a wolf!

11:50.050 --> 11:52.426
Ah um, he's almost here.

11:52.427 --> 11:53.595
Thank you.

11:53.803 --> 11:57.390
I've got another girl to take my place.
Sorry to bother you.

12:01.895 --> 12:03.896
REPLACEMENT

12:03.897 --> 12:06.190
Don't just sit there weeping like that.

12:06.191 --> 12:07.359
HUHUHUHU...

12:07.609 --> 12:09.443
Why does it have to be you?

12:09.444 --> 12:11.238
I should be the one asking that!

12:12.322 --> 12:16.201
I'm aware it was a mixer,
but it's full of familiar faces.

12:16.576 --> 12:17.618
Me too.

12:17.619 --> 12:18.286
Huh?

12:18.870 --> 12:22.207
ONLY MET THAT ONE TIMEWait, I've never met this girl before.

12:22.958 --> 12:24.793
Could she be trying to hit on me?

12:25.293 --> 12:28.213
Which means she has feelings for me...

12:38.556 --> 12:41.433
Is your "treasuring"
directed in all three directions?

12:41.434 --> 12:43.687
The chopsticks just happened to break.

12:43.812 --> 12:45.897
Let's raise our glasses first.

12:46.273 --> 12:47.941
Cheers!

12:48.441 --> 12:51.235
You guys went to my
school festival together, right?

12:51.236 --> 12:52.486
You're so close.

12:52.487 --> 12:53.780
Ah, no, we're not.

12:54.114 --> 12:55.823
Being friends with these guys...

12:55.824 --> 12:56.783
is so embarrassing!

12:56.950 --> 12:58.534
For our comrades' misfortunes,

12:58.535 --> 13:00.286
we're willing to risk our lives.

13:00.287 --> 13:01.496
Alright.

13:01.830 --> 13:03.832
Who should we target now?

13:04.749 --> 13:05.875
Short-sighted!

13:06.793 --> 13:08.086
Reckless!

13:08.586 --> 13:11.547
Of course, if I had a chance,
those two would be the best.

13:11.548 --> 13:14.509
But someone like us
could never woo them.

13:14.968 --> 13:18.346
More importantly,
if she has feelings for me...

13:22.600 --> 13:24.227
Ah, um...

13:28.481 --> 13:29.983
What's wrong, Cakey?

13:30.317 --> 13:32.443
CLACK CLACK CLACK CLACK CLACK

13:32.444 --> 13:33.485
Really, what's wrong?

13:33.486 --> 13:36.448
Did you see something
that caused a nervous breakdown?

13:36.614 --> 13:38.866
That's enough to show my feelings.

13:38.867 --> 13:39.868
Next...

13:40.076 --> 13:41.995
How do I look? Awesome, right?

13:43.413 --> 13:44.372
Ah, hey...

13:44.831 --> 13:45.790
Uh, yes.

13:47.042 --> 13:48.335
Do you like virgins?

13:48.835 --> 13:51.004
What the hell is wrong with him?!

13:51.254 --> 13:53.464
The fuck are you doing already,
you lolcow!?

13:53.465 --> 13:55.467
You ruined everything, you moron!

13:58.845 --> 14:00.971
Hmm, virgins?

14:00.972 --> 14:02.974
I think they're fine.

14:04.184 --> 14:05.476
- Goddess!
- Goddess!

14:05.477 --> 14:08.646
Come to me, little boys.

14:09.022 --> 14:10.732
What about Nanaka and the others?

14:11.024 --> 14:14.069
I'm not very familiar
with those things, so...

14:14.569 --> 14:17.822
I don't judge a person
based on that either...

14:17.947 --> 14:19.449
Not interested.

14:20.033 --> 14:21.242
Hmm.

14:22.577 --> 14:25.371
Even if I'm on my death bed,
I wouldn't want ugly virgins.

14:25.372 --> 14:26.664
- So bitter!
- So bitter!

14:26.831 --> 14:29.417
Well, she's always been like that.

14:30.001 --> 14:32.294
- Good thing I'm not ugly.
- Good thing I'm not ugly.

14:32.295 --> 14:33.922
- Incredibly optimistic!
- Incredibly optimistic!

14:34.297 --> 14:37.007
By the way, could you elaborate
on "virgins are fine"?

14:37.008 --> 14:39.676
What kind of attitude
would make a good impression?

14:39.677 --> 14:41.888
- What kind of situation are you into?
- Hold on a minute.

14:42.180 --> 14:44.723
There are some people
who don't like this topic.

14:44.724 --> 14:46.225
Talk about something normal.

14:46.226 --> 14:47.017
I apologize.

14:47.018 --> 14:48.769
I am a proper gentleman.

14:48.770 --> 14:50.480
I'll talk about normal things then.

14:57.737 --> 15:01.073
Ah, the new AV
I watched the other day was great.

15:01.074 --> 15:02.200
Oh, that one.

15:02.409 --> 15:04.119
That movie is truly amazing.

15:04.828 --> 15:06.204
I apologize.

15:06.996 --> 15:07.956
Ah, no.

15:08.623 --> 15:10.917
This blind date is really awful.

15:11.167 --> 15:13.503
Try telling an interesting story.

15:13.920 --> 15:15.880
Such a condescending tone.

15:16.423 --> 15:18.966
Kouhei, she's asking for
an interesting story.

15:18.967 --> 15:20.342
MAGICAL GIRL LALAKO
Understood.

15:20.343 --> 15:22.387
MAGICAL GIRL LALAKO
Stop wasting oxygen.

15:22.762 --> 15:25.097
Then what kind of story
would be interesting?

15:25.098 --> 15:26.433
Let's see.

15:26.850 --> 15:28.851
The story of your breakup, for instance.

15:28.852 --> 15:31.438
You really are a wicked woman.

15:31.896 --> 15:35.525
I bet you didn't even take your girlfriend
anywhere nice during summer break.

15:36.526 --> 15:37.902
That's not true.

15:38.236 --> 15:41.072
He took her to his hometown
and to Palau.

15:42.365 --> 15:46.034
So you introduced her to your family
and went on a pre-wedding trip?

15:46.035 --> 15:48.246
Ah no, it's not like that.

15:51.040 --> 15:52.417
- Huh?
- What's wrong?

15:53.042 --> 15:54.376
So pitiful.

15:54.377 --> 15:56.296
I didn't threaten her!

15:57.255 --> 15:58.506
Kitahara, Kitahara.

15:58.882 --> 15:59.924
What is it?

16:01.843 --> 16:03.886
The conversation isn't going anywhere.

16:03.887 --> 16:05.138
Huh?

16:06.055 --> 16:07.598
Solve it yourself...

16:07.599 --> 16:08.932
I'll give you 30 pornos.

16:08.933 --> 16:12.436
Well, we've been chatting
for a while now!

16:12.437 --> 16:15.105
How about we play a game
to chat a bit more?

16:15.106 --> 16:16.190
What is it? What is it?

16:16.191 --> 16:17.525
What are we playing?

16:17.734 --> 16:19.694
We'll play this.

16:19.986 --> 16:21.778
LIE DETECTOR
A lie detector?

16:21.779 --> 16:23.239
LIE DETECTOR
How does it work?

16:23.406 --> 16:25.658
It will read the changes
in your heart rate.

16:25.825 --> 16:27.618
If the needle's at this level,

16:27.619 --> 16:30.287
the machine will assume you're lying
and emit an electric shock.

16:30.288 --> 16:31.497
Does it hurt?

16:31.498 --> 16:33.166
It'll probably be a slight tingle.

16:33.333 --> 16:36.044
And the question will be on
the theme of this mixer.

16:36.294 --> 16:38.295
Is anyone here your type?

16:38.296 --> 16:39.713
Good job, Kitahara!

16:39.714 --> 16:41.006
Excellent question.

16:41.007 --> 16:43.009
It's so great being your best friend.

16:43.384 --> 16:45.845
Is there anyone I'm into
among the people here?

16:47.472 --> 16:48.223
There is.

16:51.184 --> 16:52.977
There really is.

16:53.436 --> 16:54.812
My, my.

16:55.188 --> 16:57.398
I wonder who it is?

16:59.651 --> 17:01.486
Then next is Nanaka-san.

17:01.611 --> 17:05.073
Um, as for someone here being my type...

17:05.490 --> 17:06.366
There is.

17:08.117 --> 17:09.326
Really?

17:09.327 --> 17:11.703
There is someone here who is her type!

17:11.704 --> 17:13.038
Kitahara has a girlfriend.

17:13.039 --> 17:15.249
Imamura belongs to another dimension.

17:15.250 --> 17:17.710
Then that person must be one of us.

17:17.877 --> 17:21.256
And among them,
I am the most handsome.

17:23.883 --> 17:25.300
This is tough.

17:25.301 --> 17:26.760
Today is a wonderful day.

17:26.761 --> 17:28.680
It might even turn into an anniversary.

17:29.472 --> 17:31.808
Is there someone here in the group
that's my type?

17:32.183 --> 17:33.685
No way in hell.

17:35.645 --> 17:36.479
Ouch!

17:38.314 --> 17:40.149
Hey, hey, you're lying?

17:40.316 --> 17:42.901
So there really is someone your type?

17:42.902 --> 17:45.654
Huh, isn't this toy broken?

17:45.655 --> 17:49.908
Didn't you approach Imamura
the very first time you met?

17:49.909 --> 17:52.036
He must definitely be your type.

17:52.453 --> 17:53.997
What are you talking about?

17:54.998 --> 17:57.917
As expected, this machine is very reliable.

17:58.418 --> 18:00.628
Um... there is someone.

18:01.337 --> 18:04.089
At first, she also talked to Kouhei.

18:04.090 --> 18:05.592
HA HA HA HA
So nostalgic.

18:06.092 --> 18:07.093
There isn't anyone.

18:07.302 --> 18:09.387
- Your boyfriend is right here!
- Your boyfriend is right here!

18:09.512 --> 18:11.346
This game is interesting.

18:11.347 --> 18:12.389
It really is.

18:12.390 --> 18:14.767
As expected, a mixer should be like this!

18:14.934 --> 18:16.560
Thanks, Kitahara.

18:16.561 --> 18:18.645
Thanks to you, the atmosphere is alive.

18:18.646 --> 18:20.814
You truly are my best friend.

18:20.815 --> 18:22.233
That's good then.

18:23.359 --> 18:26.988
Even though I often hang out with them,

18:27.447 --> 18:31.326
this is the first time I've seen
their faces looking so happy.

18:36.789 --> 18:39.417
So ugly it makes me want to throw up.

18:40.293 --> 18:43.211
Kouhei, it's time for us
to "deal" with them.

18:43.212 --> 18:44.839
Why all of a sudden?

18:45.006 --> 18:49.176
It's true that I promised to
organize a mixer for them.

18:49.177 --> 18:50.553
HEHEHEHEHE
Yeah, that's right.

18:51.596 --> 18:54.014
But I didn't promise
to let them return alive.

18:54.015 --> 18:56.183
I see, that makes sense.

18:56.184 --> 18:57.644
Makes sense my ass.

18:58.853 --> 19:02.397
Actually, there's no one here
who is my type.

19:02.398 --> 19:04.067
Just kidding.

19:05.318 --> 19:08.070
The shock should be quite...

19:08.071 --> 19:10.907
Why is it so strong?!

19:14.410 --> 19:15.202
Huh?

19:15.203 --> 19:16.120
Nojima?

19:16.287 --> 19:18.164
Ah, by the way...

19:18.790 --> 19:20.040
WEAK, MEDIUM, STRONG, DEATH
To liven up the atmosphere,

19:20.041 --> 19:23.378
if the guys lie, they'll be shocked
with 200 times the intensity.

19:23.586 --> 19:25.421
- Hey!
- Hey!

19:26.130 --> 19:27.005
Come on.

19:27.006 --> 19:28.549
Step up, Fujiwara.

19:28.675 --> 19:29.884
Don't mess with me.

19:30.718 --> 19:33.136
You just have to not lie.

19:33.137 --> 19:34.347
Don't be a buzzkill.

19:35.682 --> 19:38.725
As for someone here being my type...

19:38.726 --> 19:40.811
Azusa-san, you dropped your chopsticks.

19:40.812 --> 19:42.105
Ah, where?

19:42.438 --> 19:43.398
There is...

19:47.110 --> 19:48.694
Come on, step up, Yamamoto.

19:48.695 --> 19:50.445
Who would want to do that!?

19:50.446 --> 19:51.780
If we're doing this,

19:51.781 --> 19:55.992
you have to lower the voltage,
not force others to lie, and

19:55.993 --> 19:57.578
- You talk too much, die.
- guarantee safety...

20:01.708 --> 20:02.917
And that's that.

20:03.626 --> 20:06.587
That was pretty forceful, but whatever.

20:07.422 --> 20:10.591
Well then, thank you everyone
very much for today.

20:10.842 --> 20:13.886
We'll dispose of this trash ourselves.

20:14.220 --> 20:16.263
Huh? Is it over already?

20:16.264 --> 20:17.640
Haven't you had enough to drink?

20:17.765 --> 20:19.766
If so, we can head to another place...

20:19.767 --> 20:22.061
No, it's not that.

20:22.311 --> 20:23.271
This thing here.

20:23.604 --> 20:25.857
Everyone hasn't tried it yet.

20:26.524 --> 20:27.108
Huh?

20:27.525 --> 20:29.568
It wouldn't be interesting if I did it.

20:29.569 --> 20:30.986
The answer's too obvious.

20:30.987 --> 20:32.821
Now that you mention it, you said...

20:32.822 --> 20:35.407
you're looking at me and Nanaka
perversely, right?

20:35.408 --> 20:37.368
Then I'll do it.

20:38.911 --> 20:40.787
So, um...

20:40.788 --> 20:42.122
Among the people here...

20:42.123 --> 20:43.123
Wait.

20:43.124 --> 20:43.957
What is it?

20:43.958 --> 20:46.668
Knowing the answer beforehand
takes away the fun.

20:46.669 --> 20:50.506
So please answer from among
the people excluding those two.

20:50.840 --> 20:51.841
Huh?

20:51.966 --> 20:54.594
Why the sudden additional condition?

20:56.262 --> 20:58.097
It's fine, Kitahara.

20:58.556 --> 21:02.392
Thinking about a target
that's out of reach is also critical.

21:02.393 --> 21:05.021
Huh? You are the last person
I want to hear that from.

21:05.688 --> 21:08.815
But if I say "there isn't,"
then it's too simple.

21:08.816 --> 21:11.527
Look who's getting cocky.

21:11.694 --> 21:13.571
But if I say "there is" then...

21:14.197 --> 21:16.782
As expected, it's Kouhei, right?

21:16.783 --> 21:17.992
- Is that so?
- Is that so?

21:18.868 --> 21:20.787
In that case, my answer is...

21:21.037 --> 21:23.372
As for someone here being my type...

21:25.374 --> 21:26.625
There's more than one!

21:26.626 --> 21:27.877
More than one!?

21:28.169 --> 21:32.590
No, I mean everyone has
their own good points.

21:34.467 --> 21:35.968
I see.

21:36.135 --> 21:38.846
It's hard to choose just one person.

21:40.264 --> 21:42.933
Ah, then it's Kouhei's turn next.

21:42.934 --> 21:43.935
Iori-kun.

21:44.519 --> 21:45.228
Huh?

21:46.270 --> 21:47.395
So does that mean

21:47.396 --> 21:50.817
besides Chisa-chan,
you're also into someone else?

22:02.078 --> 22:04.664
Is it really okay
to leave those two like that?

22:05.206 --> 22:06.456
Don't think about it.

22:06.457 --> 22:10.253
Right now, you just need
to pray that he survives.

22:10.628 --> 22:11.963
What are you on about?

22:12.213 --> 22:14.006
It's about familial love.

22:19.637 --> 22:21.264
3... 2... 1... Go!

22:30.815 --> 22:33.567
A sweet little love story!?

22:33.568 --> 22:36.319
Asymmetrical reflection in the mirror

22:36.320 --> 22:37.946
A shattered, crunchy heart

22:37.947 --> 22:39.991
Oh oh, stumbling around

22:40.575 --> 22:42.993
Oh oh, just acting on instinct

22:42.994 --> 22:46.955
Diving deep into my subconscious

22:46.956 --> 22:48.707
Tumbling and falling down

22:48.708 --> 22:51.293
A limit-breaking paradise

22:51.294 --> 22:52.544
Viva, cheers

22:52.545 --> 22:54.004
Everyone, cheers

22:54.005 --> 22:56.047
We're in trouble, we're in trouble

22:56.048 --> 22:56.756
Big trouble

22:56.757 --> 22:58.758
We're in trouble, we're in trouble

22:58.759 --> 22:59.593
Wa wa wa

22:59.594 --> 23:01.553
We're in trouble, we're in trouble

23:01.554 --> 23:02.262
Wa wa wa wa

23:02.263 --> 23:04.222
Let's go, everybody

23:04.223 --> 23:07.684
Dramatic just like a rainbow

23:07.685 --> 23:10.687
Your troubled smile
is absolutely priceless

23:10.688 --> 23:15.984
Total chaos
getting kissed by an octopus

23:15.985 --> 23:18.737
A mermaid washed up on the shore

23:18.738 --> 23:21.656
Darling drowned down
in the Dragon Palace

23:21.657 --> 23:26.953
The treasure box is just full of alcohol

23:26.954 --> 23:29.664
The ultimate license of our youth

23:29.665 --> 23:32.626
Find the treasure and checkmate

23:32.627 --> 23:37.839
An angel who overslept
from swimming too much

23:37.840 --> 23:39.299
Let's go, everybody

23:39.300 --> 23:40.675
Viva, cheers

23:40.676 --> 23:42.010
Oh yeah

23:42.011 --> 23:43.679
Viva, cheers

23:44.931 --> 23:49.977
NEXT EPISODE: HARDSHIPS
